You're thinking that if I eat sweets, 
it'll easily make me feel happy, right?

00:14:46.730 --> 00:14:48.650
W-Well, that's not...

00:14:48.650 --> 00:14:49.720
Is she wrong?

00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:52.150
Completely wrong! How rude!

00:14:52.150 --> 00:14:54.840
It's true that I like sweets.

00:14:55.260 --> 00:14:58.460
But it's not like giving me sweets will 
always make me immediately happy.

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:02.670
Thinking of me that way, like I'm some 
little animal, is problematic for—

00:15:07.430 --> 00:15:10.650
I feel a tremendous surge of oxytocin.

00:15:10.650 --> 00:15:13.810
She becomes happy terribly 
easily, doesn't she?

00:15:13.810 --> 00:15:16.800
We need to take a saliva sample from 
her while she's in this state,

00:15:16.800 --> 00:15:19.320
and compare it to the 
previous sample, correct?

00:15:20.520 --> 00:15:21.360
Huh?

00:15:21.360 --> 00:15:23.680
Give it back!

00:15:23.680 --> 00:15:25.340
Here. Let's collect your saliva.

00:15:25.110 --> 00:15:28.190
Kanade

00:15:28.630 --> 00:15:32.890
Freshly collected saliva 
truly is so beautiful.

00:15:32.890 --> 00:15:35.280
I feel sort of embarrassed.

00:15:37.110 --> 00:15:40.950
Well, now that the saliva's been 
collected, it's our turn to work.

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:42.040
<b>Step 1</b>

00:15:41.800 --> 00:15:42.820
One.

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:46.960
<b>Step 1</b>

00:15:43.260 --> 00:15:46.710
We'll use the centrifuge to 
remove the supernatant liquid.

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:48.040
<b>Step 2</b>

00:15:47.820 --> 00:15:48.620
Two.

00:15:48.040 --> 00:15:52.960
<b>Step 2</b>

00:15:49.180 --> 00:15:51.000
Reagent and dilution.

00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:52.970
We'll apply them to the 
samples and agitate them.

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:54.050
<b>Step 3</b>

00:15:53.910 --> 00:15:54.850
Three.

00:15:54.050 --> 00:15:57.970
<b>Step 3</b>

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:57.970
We'll put them in cold storage 
to rest for 20 hours.

00:15:57.970 --> 00:15:59.050
<b>Step 4</b>

00:15:58.880 --> 00:16:00.020
Four.

00:15:59.050 --> 00:16:05.150
<b>Step 4</b>

00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:02.050
Once it's been mixed with the reagent,

00:16:02.050 --> 00:16:05.480
we can use an absorption spectrometer to 
look at the concentration of oxytocin.

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:17.450
<b>Step 4</b>

00:16:05.190 --> 00:16:17.450
<b>Step 1</b>

00:16:05.190 --> 00:16:17.450
<b>Step 3</b>

00:16:05.230 --> 00:16:17.450
<b>Step 2</b>

00:16:06.130 --> 00:16:07.980
And that completes the measurement.

00:16:08.500 --> 00:16:12.670
Other substances are measured 
in much the same way.

00:16:12.670 --> 00:16:17.060
Wow. That procedure seems 
like a lot of work.

00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:30.510
<b>Centrifuge</b>

00:16:18.270 --> 00:16:20.860
A centrifuge!

00:16:21.210 --> 00:16:22.200
Heh.

00:16:22.200 --> 00:16:24.920
You let your guard down, 
didn't you, stupid humans?!

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:30.750
I, Rikekuma-sama, 
have returned to rectify that stupidity!

00:16:31.250 --> 00:16:35.370
Starting today, I will once again be 
whipping you into shape with my teaching!

00:16:35.370 --> 00:16:38.200
Clean out your ears and 
listen closely, bear!

00:16:39.180 --> 00:16:43.360
A centrifuge applies 
strong centrifugal force

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:47.860
<b>Centrifugal force</b>

00:16:43.360 --> 00:16:49.750
to separate out the tiny particles and 
substances of different weights from the liquid.

00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:51.530
It's an amazing machine, bear!

00:16:51.730 --> 00:16:54.420
The one they use here is 
a centrifugal peni—

00:16:55.340 --> 00:16:57.050
A centrifugal precipitation machine.

00:16:57.050 --> 00:17:00.330
It spins the vessels containing 
the liquid around and around,

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:03.690
and sinks the specified substances 
to the bottom, bear.

00:17:05.460 --> 00:17:08.080
There are also things called 
centrifugal dehydrators.

00:17:08.080 --> 00:17:12.650
You put materials inside a cylinder 
which is full of tiny holes,

00:17:12.650 --> 00:17:14.360
spin it around and around,

00:17:14.360 --> 00:17:17.770
and centrifugal force drives 
out just the water, bear.

00:17:18.590 --> 00:17:23.170
In short, it's the drying function 
in a washing machine, bear.

00:17:23.170 --> 00:17:25.800
All you blasted humans who 
wanna become science-types...

00:17:26.220 --> 00:17:29.910
"Man, lately I've been using 
centrifuges every day!"

00:17:29.910 --> 00:17:31.920
"It's really hard to control them!"

00:17:31.920 --> 00:17:35.160
That's what you should be saying while 
you're using your washing machine, bear.

00:17:35.770 --> 00:17:38.570
So the measurements, at your 
quickest, will take a day?

00:17:38.570 --> 00:17:41.580
That's a lot faster than sending it out.

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:42.680
Yes.

00:17:42.680 --> 00:17:45.830
We can examine as much 
saliva as we like here.

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:48.990
Well, let's get straight 
to it. How does your love,

00:17:48.990 --> 00:17:52.070
compare to ours, that of a couple.

00:17:52.420 --> 00:17:54.480
Let's begin the experiment, shall we?

00:17:54.720 --> 00:17:57.470
<b>Experiment      1</b>

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:57.470
<b>"Say what you like about the other person</b>

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:57.470
<b>to increase happiness values."</b>

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:57.470
<b>Chris-Fujiwara pair</b>

00:17:58.210 --> 00:18:00.150
Oh, Sui!

00:18:00.150 --> 00:18:03.840
I could never say as much as I want to 
say of the things I love about you!

00:18:03.840 --> 00:18:07.720
You are as graceful as a 
fresh breeze over a lake!

00:18:08.210 --> 00:18:12.910
You are as beautiful as the red valerian 
that blooms on Cornwall's grassy fields!

00:18:12.910 --> 00:18:15.630
Yukimura-han, you're in 
information sciences, right?

00:18:15.630 --> 00:18:17.350
You're quite handsome.

00:18:17.350 --> 00:18:20.610
We don't have your type in our department.

00:18:21.420 --> 00:18:22.240
Wha?!

00:18:22.250 --> 00:18:26.190
Sui! You're exposing your skin to 
someone of the opposite sex again!

00:18:26.190 --> 00:18:30.010
What will you do if he jumps 
on you like a savage beast?!

00:18:30.490 --> 00:18:31.610
Savage beast?

00:18:33.240 --> 00:18:34.620
Say, Chris...

00:18:34.620 --> 00:18:35.490
Huh?

00:18:37.270 --> 00:18:43.760
I like the way you always say things to me 
like "I love you" or "you're beautiful."

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:49.270
And when I bare my skin, the way you 
panic and come to rescue me is adorable.

00:18:49.680 --> 00:18:50.830
I love it.

00:18:52.330 --> 00:18:55.470
I-I also... You...

00:18:55.470 --> 00:18:57.520
Yes. Say it more.

00:18:57.520 --> 00:18:59.720
Um, I mean...

00:18:59.720 --> 00:19:03.900
You are as graceful as a 
fresh breeze over a lake...

00:19:03.900 --> 00:19:06.780
Like the valerian in Cornwall...

00:19:07.050 --> 00:19:09.320
<i>Their besotted-couple-power is incredible!</i>

00:19:09.320 --> 00:19:13.300
<i>What can we do against this oxytocin aura?</i>

00:19:13.540 --> 00:19:15.800
<b>Experiment     2</b>

00:19:14.090 --> 00:19:15.800
<b>"Say what you like about the other person</b>

00:19:14.090 --> 00:19:15.800
<b>to increase happiness values."</b>

00:19:14.090 --> 00:19:15.800
<b>Yukimura-Himuro pair</b>

00:19:18.350 --> 00:19:21.420
I've complied the points 
I find likable about you.

00:19:21.420 --> 00:19:22.920
This is the third edition.

00:19:22.920 --> 00:19:26.490
I've added, "He's fast at 
calculating Fourier transforms."

00:19:26.490 --> 00:19:30.700
And I've added, "When she cleans the 
source code, everything's easier to see."

00:19:32.310 --> 00:19:35.030
This is bad. 
It's too similar to our everyday.

00:19:35.030 --> 00:19:37.810
I'm not feeling the least bit happier.

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:46.550
Yukimura-kun, say something 
that will make me feel happy.

00:19:46.550 --> 00:19:48.120
Like Chris-senpai did.

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:48.960
Huh?!

00:19:49.530 --> 00:19:51.740
<i>What do I do?</i>

00:19:51.740 --> 00:19:54.910
<i>Should I use some kind of metaphor 
and speak in a poetic way?</i>

00:19:58.120 --> 00:20:01.220
Himuro... Lately you...

00:20:01.220 --> 00:20:04.140
you've been as beautiful 
as the Perseus cluster...

00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:06.030
redolent of ethyl formate...

00:20:06.030 --> 00:20:08.320
as great as the cosmos...

00:20:08.320 --> 00:20:09.600
I have no idea what that means.

00:20:09.600 --> 00:20:13.150
By that, do you mean that I'm 
expanding like the universe?!

00:20:13.150 --> 00:20:14.600
I do not!

00:20:14.850 --> 00:20:17.360
<b>Experiment   3</b>

00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:17.360
<b>"While alone in a locked room together, make physical contact</b>

00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:17.360
<b>to increase happiness values."</b>

00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:17.360
<b>Chris-Fujiwara pair</b>

00:20:20.170 --> 00:20:23.980
Physical contact with your partner 
is the key to producing oxytocin.

00:20:24.380 --> 00:20:27.360
Here in this locked room, 
we should flirt and cuddle as we like

00:20:27.360 --> 00:20:30.360
as an experiment to see how it 
will affect our oxytocin levels.

00:20:30.360 --> 00:20:31.920
Which means...

00:20:33.100 --> 00:20:37.440
we two will be alone together in a 
tiny room where no one can see us.

00:20:37.440 --> 00:20:40.480
That means we can do whatever we want.

00:20:40.480 --> 00:20:42.250
Wha—?! Sui?

00:20:42.820 --> 00:20:46.470
Chris, I can't hold myself back any longer.

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:48.290
Let's hurry up and feel good together.

00:20:48.290 --> 00:20:50.350
W-Wait, please, Sui!

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:51.510
You really mean to do it here?!

00:20:51.510 --> 00:20:55.140
Why not? After all, 
no one will be able to see us.

00:20:55.140 --> 00:20:57.630
Even so! Regardless of the 
circumstances, that's just...

00:20:57.630 --> 00:20:59.440
You can't get away anymore.

00:21:02.590 --> 00:21:04.540
No, not there!

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:07.650
<i>Is R-18 stuff okay?!</i>

00:21:07.990 --> 00:21:11.670
<i>I don't really understand, 
but couples are amazing!</i>

00:21:11.940 --> 00:21:16.910
<i>I can't even imagine. 
What is happening in there?!</i>

00:21:21.290 --> 00:21:22.650
It's no good.

00:21:22.920 --> 00:21:24.930
How am I supposed to 
endure something like that?

00:21:24.930 --> 00:21:28.280
As a knight, as a man... I'm a failure.

00:21:28.280 --> 00:21:31.070
If it felt good, then it's fine, isn't it?

00:21:32.430 --> 00:21:34.680
<b>Experiment   4</b>

00:21:32.980 --> 00:21:34.680
<b>"While alone in a locked room together, make physical contact</b>

00:21:32.980 --> 00:21:34.680
<b>to increase happiness values."</b>

00:21:32.980 --> 00:21:34.680
<b>Yukimura-Himuro pair</b>

00:21:36.400 --> 00:21:37.850
So, what do we do?

00:21:38.230 --> 00:21:42.090
They're giving the definite impression 
that they're building up oxytocin.

00:21:42.090 --> 00:21:44.320
At this rate, we have no way of winning.

00:21:44.800 --> 00:21:48.570
We must think of some way to produce 
large amounts of oxytocin.

00:21:49.010 --> 00:21:52.060
A way to produce large 
amounts of oxytocin...

00:21:56.010 --> 00:21:59.070
<i>I want to kiss one more time.</i>

00:22:03.080 --> 00:22:07.470
Th-Thinking about it logically, 
that's the only option, right?

00:22:07.980 --> 00:22:11.300
After that is when we had our 
highest levels of oxytocin.

00:22:11.730 --> 00:22:14.980
At the present time, it is likely 
the most efficient method.

00:22:15.660 --> 00:22:21.580
You know, this time, nothing should be 
rough from salt like last time, so...

00:22:22.140 --> 00:22:23.220
I know.

00:22:38.460 --> 00:22:40.770
Those are the results of 
yesterday's experiments.

00:22:40.770 --> 00:22:41.840
Impossible!

00:22:42.230 --> 00:22:46.620
You completely beat our oxytocin 
levels in every single experiment?!

00:22:46.620 --> 00:22:49.270
It can't be. 
What was the highest value?

00:22:49.260 --> 00:22:53.890
<b>Experiment 5 While alone in a locked room together, make physical contact to increase happiness values.
Oxytocin | Fujiwara | Chris | Oxytocin | Himuro | Yukimura
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h646 → 847 pg/mL | 516 → 1129 pg/mL                                          413 → 472 pg/mL | 252 → 307pg/mL</b>

00:22:49.540 --> 00:22:53.900
It seems that the locked room 
had the highest levels, but...

00:22:53.900 --> 00:22:57.460
both the absolute values and the amount of 
change are an order of magnitude higher!

00:22:57.460 --> 00:23:00.390
That can't be true. 
We even went so far as to kiss!

00:23:00.390 --> 00:23:03.390
What? You kissed? In that room?

00:23:03.640 --> 00:23:06.660
What method could they possibly have used?

00:23:16.330 --> 00:23:18.920
Y-You used her lap as a pillow?!

00:23:19.140 --> 00:23:23.300
If that was all, then how could you 
have produced so much oxytocin?!

00:23:23.300 --> 00:23:25.900
I told you, didn't I, Yukimura-kun?

00:23:25.900 --> 00:23:28.920
This is what a real couple is.

00:23:29.660 --> 00:23:30.930
<i>Think.</i>

00:23:31.300 --> 00:23:33.030
<i>There must be something!</i>

00:23:33.350 --> 00:23:34.600
<i>Think!</i>

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:39.930
Next Time

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:39.930
Proof 2
Science-types Fell in Love, 
So They Tried Looking for a New Theory.

00:23:35.320 --> 00:23:36.880
Next time, Proof 2...

00:23:36.880 --> 00:23:39.980
